WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.562
Orchard Core shows hundreds of technical time zone names.

00:00:04.562 --> 00:00:08.860
This video shows how the Time Zones feature replaces them with a short

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.461
list of friendly names that you control:

00:00:11.461 --> 00:00:14.910
why it exists, how to add a name, how to set the site's

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:18.020
time zone, and how each person can use their own.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.466
Every date and time on your site is shown in some time zone,

00:00:26.466 --> 00:00:28.506
and someone has to choose it:

00:00:28.506 --> 00:00:31.070
the site, a team member, or a contact.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.430
Out of the box, the menu lists hundreds of technical names, such as

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.525
America slash Argentina slash Buenos Aires.

00:00:39.525 --> 00:00:44.640
They are hard to scan, and most of them are zones nobody on your team uses.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:49.495
People pick the wrong one, or pick different names for the same place,

00:00:49.495 --> 00:00:52.520
and times shown to customers and colleagues drift.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:56.692
With the Time Zones feature, you decide the list.

00:00:56.692 --> 00:01:01.483
Every menu shows only your friendly names, such as Eastern Time, in the

00:01:01.483 --> 00:01:03.350
same order for everyone.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:11.979
A time zone map is a friendly name linked to one real time zone.

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:14.130
The name is what people see.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.166
The feature starts with about twenty common maps from around the world.

00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:22.060
You can edit or delete them, and add your own.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:27.076
Once the feature is on, every time zone menu shows only the names

00:01:27.076 --> 00:01:29.600
on this list, in alphabetical order:

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.107
the site's default time zone, a person's own time zone, and the menus

00:01:34.107 --> 00:01:36.390
on contact and activity screens.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.692
A zone that has no map cannot be picked anywhere.

00:01:40.692 --> 00:01:44.050
If a menu is missing a zone, add a map for it.

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:50.287
Open Tools, Time Zones.

00:01:50.287 --> 00:01:52.069
Each row is one map:

00:01:52.069 --> 00:01:56.868
its name, the time zone it stands for, who created it, and when.

00:01:56.868 --> 00:01:59.679
The Search box finds a map by name.

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:08.446
Click Add Time Zone Map.

00:02:08.446 --> 00:02:12.865
The Name is what people will see, for example Mexico City Time.

00:02:13.363 --> 00:02:19.868
Choose the Time zone the name stands for, here America slash Mexico City, and click Save.

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:25.003
Each name can be used once, and each time zone can have only one map.

00:02:25.454 --> 00:02:27.497
The new map is on the list.

00:02:27.497 --> 00:02:30.530
Edit points a map at a different time zone.

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:34.369
The name is fixed after you save it, so to rename a map,

00:02:34.369 --> 00:02:36.474
delete it and add a new one.

00:02:40.719 --> 00:02:44.517
The site's time zone is used to show dates and times to everyone

00:02:44.517 --> 00:02:46.416
who has not picked their own.

00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:47.989
Open Settings, General.

00:02:48.518 --> 00:02:52.588
Default Time Zone now offers only your friendly names.

00:02:52.588 --> 00:02:56.388
Choose one, here Mexico City Time, and click Save.

00:03:00.654 --> 00:03:05.599
When your administrator turns on the User Time Zone feature, each person can

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:07.769
have a time zone of their own.

00:03:07.769 --> 00:03:10.904
Open Access Control, Users, and edit a person.

00:03:11.389 --> 00:03:17.264
The Default Time Zone menu lists the same friendly names, and Use site's time zone.

00:03:17.264 --> 00:03:20.763
Choose one, here India Standard Time, and save.

00:03:20.763 --> 00:03:25.119
From then on, this person sees dates and times in that zone.

00:03:25.611 --> 00:03:29.111
People who do not choose one see the site's time zone.

00:03:33.311 --> 00:03:38.331
A team spread over a few offices, who should all pick from the same short list.

00:03:39.081 --> 00:03:44.821
A site that shows event, delivery or opening times to visitors in the right local time.

00:03:45.571 --> 00:03:51.331
A contact center, where agents set the time zone of each contact and activity.

00:03:52.081 --> 00:03:58.561
One consistent name for each place, such as Eastern Time, instead of several technical ones.

00:04:00.561 --> 00:04:04.601
Add a name for each time zone you use, choose the site's default,

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.649
and let people pick their own.

00:04:06.649 --> 00:04:10.461
Every menu then offers the same short list of friendly names.

00:04:10.461 --> 00:04:11.941
Thanks for watching.

